 - **neo-tree.nvim**, **nvim-tree.lua**, **fzf-lua**, **which-key.nvim**, **snacks.nvim** all follow the same pattern: define their own groups with `default = true`, link to `Normal`, `NormalFloat`, `FloatBorder`, `Pmenu`, `Visual`, `Comment`, `Directory`, `Special`, `DiagnosticError/Warn/Info/Hint`, `Diff*`/`Added`/`Changed`/`Removed`.

9. **Version differences matter**: 0.10 introduced `Added`, `Changed`, `Removed`, `WinBar`, `WinBarNC`, `SnippetTabstop`, and renamed many `@text.*` Treesitter captures to `@markup.*`. 0.11 added `PmenuMatch`, `PmenuMatchSel`, `LspReferenceTarget`, virtual-line diagnostics groups (`DiagnosticVirtualLines{Error,Warn,Info,Hint,Ok}`), and changed the `Pmenu*` cascade so `PmenuSel` and `PmenuMatch` inherit from `Pmenu`. 0.12 added `DiffTextAdd`, the `update` flag for `nvim_set_hl`, `'winborder'` and `'pumborder'` options, the new SGR attributes (`dim`/`blink`/`conceal`/`overline`), and the experimental `vim._core.ui2` cmdline.

