## Caveats

- Some specific facts about exact default-link tables (`hl_map` in `treesitter/highlighter.lua`, the full `highlight_init_both`/`highlight_init_dark`/`highlight_init_light` arrays in `src/nvim/highlight_group.c`) shift between Neovim versions. The list above is consolidated from the 0.10–0.12 source and `:h treesitter-highlight-groups`, `:h hl-*` tags, and `:h lsp-semantic_tokens`, but you should run `:hi` and `:Inspect` on your target Neovim version to verify before shipping.
- The `@lsp.type.* → @<treesitter>` default links shipped in core have evolved. As of 0.10/0.11, `@lsp.type.parameter → @variable.parameter`, `@lsp.type.property → @variable.member`, `@lsp.type.namespace → @module`, `@lsp.type.method → @function.method` (the deprecated `@parameter`, `@field`, `@namespace`, `@method` are aliased). On 0.9 the older names were used; provide both for backward compat.
- "Plugin-agnostic" is an ideal, not a guarantee. A small minority of plugins (older or stylistic ones) hardcode their colors with `default = false`, ignoring user themes. The list of supported plugins in tokyonight (~70+) and catppuccin (~50+) integrations is roughly the long tail of plugins that *don't* respect the link convention. For mainstream, recently-maintained plugins (the ones used in LazyVim, AstroNvim, NvChad, kickstart) the link-via-`default=true` convention is universal.
- Neovim 0.12 (released March 2026) and 0.13 are still seeing default-colorscheme/highlight-group adjustments; the `vim._core.ui2` cmdline UI is experimental and subject to change. Treat any 0.12-only highlight as "best-effort" and gate it with `has('nvim-0.12')` so users on 0.10/0.11 don't see errors.
- Some search results referenced were summarized via secondary documentation sites (DeepWiki, Mintlify mirrors of Neovim docs) when the canonical source was unfetchable; the structural and naming details were corroborated against the official `neovim/neovim` GitHub source (`runtime/doc/news-0.10.txt`, `news-0.11.txt`, `news-0.12.txt`, `runtime/doc/diagnostic.txt`, `src/nvim/highlight_group.c`) and the upstream READMEs for tokyonight, catppuccin, gitsigns, nvim-cmp, and telescope.